{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1543211-fighting-style-heavy-weapons-bug","id":1543211,"title":"Fighting style - Heavy Weapons. Bug?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-06T13:37:08-07:00","id":1543211,"title":"Fighting style - Heavy Weapons. Bug?","content":"In Chronicles of Darkness, second edition, there is a Heavy Weapons fighting style merit. The first degree goes like this: Sure Strike (\u2022): Your character doesn\u2019t always hit the hardest or the most frequently, but you guarantee a deadly strike when you do hit. You can reflexively remove three dice from any attack dice pool (to a minimum of zero) to add one to your character\u2019s weapon damage rating for the turn. These dice must be removed after calculating any penalties from the environment or the opponent\u2019s Defense.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that it grants no advantage: The three dice that are removed from the dicepool make on average 1 success. However, an extra success in the roll to hit the target is also added to the damage. It therefore seems to me that using the Sure Strike is strictly weaker than not using it. This is because I am removing (on average) one success from the throw to hit the target, which would also contribute to damage. Sure Strike gives me one success, which gives me back the success I lost on sacrificing the three dice, but only conditionally on hitting the target.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:48:08-07:00","id":1543215,"title":"","content":"No, you're not missing anything. If combined with other Merits that interacts with your weapon's damage rating, you could theoretically get some use off of it, but that's highly dependent on weird and most probably unintended synergies.<br /> On its own, it's just bad. In the theoretical situation where you've lost 10 Again you could argue that it would increase your average damage, but only by a fraction and only if you have enough dice that losing three wouldn't meaningfully impact your chance of hitting the enemy (in which case that fraction of a damage wouldn't meaningfully matter anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T16:07:32-07:00","id":1543225,"title":"","content":"Trading three thirds of a success for a guaranteed extra success on two-handed weapons that apply an Initiative penalty in exchange for higher base damage means you have access to a maneuver that is the gamble it describes, which may make the difference between allowing an attacker to take another turn. It's a one-dot effect as the entry-level benefit of a Style built around big swings.<br /> <br /> It also provides setup for Warding Stance, which explicitly keys off of your weapon damage for the turn.<br /> <br /> More generally speaking, it's important to remember that the average successes per die is not the same thing as the odds of getting that many successes. The difference is small, but <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Probability_Math\" target=\"_blank\">the odds of rolling two successes with 10-Again are consistently lower than those of rolling one success with three fewer dice</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T07:45:42-07:00","id":1543339,"title":"","content":"Thank you for responses! I am tempted to modify it to add more benefit from the maneuver. Do you have a favorite home rule for it? For example, only subtract two dices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T14:35:24-07:00","id":1543360,"title":"","content":"If you want to homebrew, I think you'd have a better effect making new effects that key from base damage instead. Make it indirectly more valuable as raising base damage gives off some few extra benefits.<br /> <br /> As Satchel said, it is actually already balanced to its position, and the math isn't as straightforward as it seems. While the average success of a roll is 33% per die, the likelihood of a success on a die is actually plain 30%, so those three dice aren\u2019t as likely to give an extra success as it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T03:36:04-07:00","id":1543409,"title":"","content":"Another thing, in my experience it happens often to roll a chance die because enemy defence is very high.<br /> In those cases reducing the pool results in a chance die anyway, but with +1damage<br /> (All of this excluding willpower rules)<br /> Once you know that an enemy has such an high defence you use Sure strike every turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T13:59:16-07:00","id":1543537,"title":"","content":"In the end, I wrote a simple <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/VNHeCmUj\" target=\"_blank\">simulator of combat</a> to find out. (There might be bugs! Corrections welcome.) The results:<br /> <br /> 2 equal persons ('Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1) with knife and no armor, one uses the maneuver, the other not:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 89%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 22%</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 22%</span></b><br /> <br /> with knife, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 49%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 37%</span>\u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 11%</span></b><br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 55%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 44%</span>\u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 29%</span></b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 80%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 68% </span>\u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 48%</span></b>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> So it seems the maneuver gives serious disadvantage, only in case when the opponent is heavily armored and the protagonist is equipped with really heavy armor, it is cca 50%-50%. In those situations, I guess combination with other maneuvers might bring extra advantage, but without that, it almost seems like with two dice penalty it would be better balanced.<br /> <br /> P.S. the percentage is the percentage of the person doing the maneuver winning in fight until one is unconcious or dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T16:29:57-07:00","id":1543558,"title":"","content":"Run simulations between dissimilar combatants to see how it affects distinct scenarios.<br /> <br /> What happens when the user has more dice to attack? And less? What happens when their opponent has more or less dice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T09:28:53-07:00","id":1543585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1543211-fighting-style-heavy-weapons-bug?p=1543537#post1543537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I wrote a simple <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/VNHeCmUj\" target=\"_blank\">simulator of combat</a> to find out. (There might be bugs! Corrections welcome.) The results:<br /> <br /> 2 equal persons ('Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1) with knife and no armor, one uses the maneuver, the other not:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 89%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 22%</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 22%</span></b><br /> <br /> with knife, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 49%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 37%</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 11%</span></b><br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 55%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 44%</span>\u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 29%</span></b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Not using maneuver: 50%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 99%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 80%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 68% </span>\u200b<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 48%</span></b>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> So it seems the maneuver gives serious disadvantage, only in case when the opponent is heavily armored and the protagonist is equipped with really heavy armor, it is cca 50%-50%. In those situations, I guess combination with other maneuvers might bring extra advantage, but without that, it almost seems like with two dice penalty it would be better balanced.<br /> <br /> P.S. the percentage is the percentage of the person doing the maneuver winning in fight until one is unconcious or dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your simulation is interesting, but it's not accurate to the game or real life. You're not giving up 75% of your dice pool on the attack to try and do an extra 30% damage (or whatever). Run your simulation again with combat PC stats, probably a dicepool of 9 or so and see who wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T13:34:19-07:00","id":1543628,"title":"","content":"Some more simulations:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Protagonist (using the maneuver): {'Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1}</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Antagonist: {'Strength': 1, 'Dexterity': 1, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1}</span>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 95%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 98%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 97%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 96%\u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 93%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 99.7%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 100%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 100%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 99.9% \u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 99.8%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Protagonist (using the maneuver): {'Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1}</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Antagonist: {'Strength': 4, 'Dexterity': 4, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 4, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 4}</span>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 16.8%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 26.1%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 18.1%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 9.7%\u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 3.6%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 3.7%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 30.4%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 19.2%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 8.8% \u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 2.4%</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For simplicity, modelling willpower spending as permanent +3 bonus, since the combat is rarely longer than 10 rounds. This is also in direction of larger pools.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Protagonist (using the maneuver): {'Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Antagonist: {'Strength': 1, 'Dexterity': 1, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 83.9%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 91.5%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 89.2%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 86.5%\u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 82.9%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 94.6%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 98.7%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 98.3%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 97.4% \u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 96.1%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Protagonist (using the maneuver): {'Strength': 3, 'Dexterity': 3, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 3, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 1, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Antagonist: {'Strength': 4, 'Dexterity': 4, 'Stamina': 3, 'Wits': 4, 'Composure': 3, 'Weaponry': 4, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 23.1%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 35.1%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 29.3%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 23.0%\u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 16.8%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 12.4%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 36.3%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 29.2%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 21.4% \u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 13.9%</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Protagonist (using the maneuver): {'Strength': 5, 'Dexterity': 5, 'Stamina': 5, 'Wits': 5, 'Composure': 5, 'Weaponry': 5, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Antagonist: {'Strength': 5, 'Dexterity': 5, 'Stamina': 5, 'Wits': 5, 'Composure': 5, 'Weaponry': 5, 'WP': 3}</span>\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> with fire ax, no armor:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 50.0%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 60.5%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 57.0%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 53.0%\u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 50.0%</b>\u200b<br /> <br /> with fire ax, both wearing full riot gear:<br /> <br /> Not using maneuver: 50.0%<br /> +1 dmg, no dice subtracted: 70.6%<br /> +1 dmg, -1 dice subtracted: 66.5%<br /> +1 dmg, -2 dice subtracted: 61.0% \u200b<br /> <b>+1 dmg, -3 dice subtracted: 55.0%</b>\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T05:10:52-07:00","id":1543744,"title":"","content":"As discussed early in the thread - this isn't the full picture. There are other things which key off of the damage rating you got(and even higher dots of the same style) which gives other advantages. Yeah, in isolation this merit, at 1 dot is questionable. Someone focused for combat will rarely just take 1 dot of a combat style merit. And hey, not all merits are made equal - this one is clearly made with the other stuff in mind to make it actually shine. <br /> <br /> When trying to balance, you also have to take into account what happens when someone specialized takes the full benefit of this, by taking synergetic choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T10:28:39-07:00","id":1543766,"title":"","content":"The simulation shows a 5% increase in win percentage when used by a decent combatant against another decent combatant. That's fairly significant for 1 xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}